# DTF tier manifest: scan-on-proxy-pub-conan  (artifact-keeper 1.12.0: #4107
# Pub, #4108 Conan, epic #4097)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream (a Pub repository
# and a Conan v2 server whose packages carry known identities). LOCAL-ONLY:
# the verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its pre-seeded
# vulnerability DB (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: before 1.12.0 a Pub or Conan Remote (or a Virtual over one)
# with scan_on_proxy=true streamed every proxied archive unscanned (200, no
# X-AK-Scan) and /api/v1/formats reported both as `accepted`. 1.12.0 routes
# Pub package archives and the Conan .tgz recipe/package archives through the
# shared inline scan gate: vulnerable -> 403 scan_blocked, clean -> 200
# X-AK-Scan: clean with the verdict reused, an archive that does not back the
# request -> 423 under fail_closed with no verdict row, fail_open -> served
# pending then blocked once the async verdict lands; Conan text files and the
# Pub JSON API stay unscanned.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.5. Green: an image carrying artifact-keeper#4107-#4108.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
